# vdrsternelec release servers
# Format: [!]type|name|url|channel|filter
#   type    json   = LibreELEC style server with releases.json
#           github = GitHub releases, url is owner/repo
#           index  = plain HTTP directory listing
#           dir    = local or mounted network directory, url is the path
#           smb    = Samba share, url is smb://[[domain;]user[:password]@]server/share/path
#           dir and smb use a releases.json in the directory if there is one
#   channel channel (json, dir, smb) or text contained in the tag (github), empty = all
#   filter  optional regular expression for file names
#   A leading '!' disables an entry.

# Official VDR*ELEC releases (all distributions, matched by device)
github|VDR*ELEC|Zabrimus/VDRSternELEC||

# Only LibreELEC 13 based releases
!github|VDR*ELEC LE13|Zabrimus/VDRSternELEC|LibreELEC-13|

# Own builds with a releases.json
!json|My builds|https://builds.example.org/vdrelec/||

# Update files in a directory on the NAS (via HTTP)
!index|NAS|http://192.168.1.10/vdrelec/||

# Update files in a local directory, on a USB stick or a mounted network
# share (manual update), checksums in <file>.sha256 or SHA256SUMS
!dir|USB stick|/var/media/USBSTICK/updates||

# Samba share (directly, no mount needed), with user and password
!smb|NAS (Samba)|smb://user:secret@nas/vdr/updates||
